## The problem

In a factory, the camera can be fooled by a wrong object, and the wire to the controller can be tampered with. Most systems only guard one of the two.

## The approach

YOLO11n on a plain CPU decides accept or reject. The command to the STM32 is encrypted with AES-128-CTR and signed with HMAC-SHA256, so a forged or replayed command is dropped.

## What I'd do next

Move inference onto an edge board and test against a live attacker on the bus.
